CrystalHD Settings translation catalogues
=======================================

The optional GTK frontend loads the crystalhd-settings gettext domain from
DATADIR/locale. GNU gettext tools are needed to update/check catalogues and
msgfmt is needed by make install-settings. No gettext tools are needed at run
time. Python's gettext honours LANGUAGE, LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES and LANG; missing
translations fall back to the English source strings. GTK's own stock controls
also depend on the host's GTK translations.

Run make settings-pot after changing a literal _("...") message in
scripts/crystalhd-settings.py. This combines a static UTF-8 header with xgettext
output in source order, without paths or generated timestamps. Update a catalogue with:

    msgmerge --no-fuzzy-matching --update --backup=none po/ko.po po/crystalhd-settings.pot
    make settings-l10n-check

The check also compares all extracted msgids with Python's source literals,
including Unicode punctuation and mathematical symbols, to catch encoding loss.

Add new locale names to po/LINGUAS. Keep configuration keys, literal values,
profile names and environment-variable names unchanged. An underscore marks a
keyboard mnemonic; keep one mnemonic in translations where the source has one,
and review for collisions on the same page. Review complete messages in context,
including warnings about application restarts and acknowledged experiments.

Korean status: all 150 current supported POT messages have Korean translations.
Review record (2026-10-31): a separate Codex agent independently reviewed every
translation against the POT, GTK settings-editor source and configuration guide,
and resolved its findings before removing the fuzzy flags. This is an agent
source-context review, not a claim of human approval. Review covered Korean
wording, setting precedence, save/reload warnings, experimental-launch
acknowledgements, numeric limits, literal identifiers and formatting (including
whitespace on joined prefixes/suffixes). Latin keyboard mnemonics use forms such
as 저장(_S); 출력 크기 값 uses (_Z) from size to avoid the expanded profile
section's 편집할 설정(_E) mnemonic on the same page. Profile-selection
inheritance, installation-completion records and several status/help messages
were clarified during review.

The check target validates fuzzy entries as well as active translations. Normal
installation never uses --use-fuzzy: reviewed entries are active once their
fuzzy flags are removed, and fuzzy or missing entries fall back to English.
Install tests exercise active Korean, an unknown locale and a separate fuzzy
fixture without substituting the fixture for the actual Korean catalogue.

Core diagnostics, installation report text, preset metadata and Desktop Entry
translations are outside this catalogue's current scope. The review record above
covers the Korean messages in this catalogue. Screen-reader usability, manual
desktop acceptance and native i386 runtime acceptance have separate checks;
catalogue review and validation do not replace those checks.
